## Sites (read, not driven under zh-CN)

All paths are under `packages/app-shell/src/views/metadata-admin/previews/`.

1. **`DashboardPreview.tsx`**, whose add trigger reads zh once PR objectui#10832 lands (添加组件):
   - the empty canvas's `PreviewMessage`: "Add at least one widget to see a preview.";
   - the `PreviewErrorBoundary` `fallbackHint`: "A widget references an object or field that doesn't resolve.";
   - the `SelectedWidgetBar`'s "Selected";
   - the aria-labels "Save title", "Rename widget" and "Clear selection";
   - the title "Click to rename".
2. **`simulator/flow-simulator.ts`**, the Debug run's step notes. The file makes zero catalogue reads, and every step note is English:
   - "Screen reached — provide inputs, then continue.";
   - "Wait reached — continue manually.";
   - "Screen has no input — …";
   - the screen step's frame around the unevaluable `visibleWhen` reasons: "A screen field's visibleWhen may reference only the fields declared on this screen; …".

## Why it matters

A zh-CN author sees Chinese headings and pickers beside English notes on the same canvas. This is the objectui#10586 / objectui#10696 / objectui#10748 / objectui#10804 family. Per objectui#10804's triage (`5858042322`), a designer surface later found in English under zh-CN rides on the family's open closure card. Once objectui#10804 closes, this card is that carrier.

## Direction (for triage to confirm)

The objectui#10804 shape:
- `engine.*` rows whose en value equals today's literal, plus zh;
- a designer-locale seam (`useMetadataLocale`), threaded into the simulator's step notes;
- one zh pin per site through the real component, with an en control. Per the role file's rule on hint wording, read the en row with `t(key,'en-US')` rather than pinning the literal (the objectui#10748 pin shape).

Also carry the objectui#10832 review's follow-up: its en controls for `engine.flowRef.notAScreenField*` pin literal hint wording. Switch them to `tFormat(key, 'en-US', …)`.

⛔ Stored author data (widget titles such as `New bar chart`) stays literal, per objectui#10678 / objectui#10651.

Serial: after PR objectui#10832 (objectui#10804) merges, since it edits files in the same directory.

